===Adjective===
{{en-adj|higher-octane|sup=highest-octane}}

# {{lb|en|of fuel}} Having a high [[octane number]], good [[antiknock]] [[characteristic]]s; used in [[high-performance]] [[vehicle]]s.
#: {{ant|en|low-octane}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=w:Terry Hayes; w:George Miller|year=1982|title=Mad Max 2: The Road Warrior|role=Max|actor=Mel Gibson|passage=Now, to do the job, I need some '''high-octane''' gasoline.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} High powered, [[energetic]], [[forceful]] or [[dynamic]].
#: {{ant|en|low-octane}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2008|month=January–February|author=Matt Bean|title=Your cultural calendar: 7 things to look forward to this year|journal=w:Men's Health|volume=23|issue=1|issn=1054-4836|page={{gbooks|6ccDAAAAMBAJ|135|high-octane}}|passage=So what if the Greeks never had BMX bikes? This year's Olympic Games, which kick off August 8 in China, add '''high-octane''' competitions—BMX racing and open-water swimming—and include sports like table tennis taken to Olympian levels.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Owen Gibson|title=Is the unthinkable happening – are people finally switching the football off?|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2016/oct/24/sky-sports-bt-sport-people-switching-football-off|newspaper=w:The Guardian|location=London|date=24 October 2016|passage=Will the exponential growth in TV rights income at home and abroad that has fuelled the endless inflation of the Premier League’s '''high-octane''' balloon ever level off?}}
# {{lb|en|of drinks}} Highly [[intoxicating]] or [[caffeinated]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=j6B2CQAAQBAJ&pg=PT103&dq=%22high-octane%22+beer&hl=&cd=7&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22high-octane%22%20beer&f=false|author=Josh Christie|title=Maine Beer: Brewing in Vacationland|publisher=Arcadia Publishing|isbn=9781614238898|text=There's no question that the '''high-octane''' beers of Marshall Wharf have had a massive influence on the breweries that have opened in Maine since 2007.}}

